      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2013. Published by Elsevier Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "The \"Crush\" procedure is a 2-stent technique for the treatment of bifurcation lesions with greater rates of in-stent restenosis than the Culotte technique. In conclusion, we report a possible mechanism for this discrepancy in the case of severe Crush stent fracture with associated focal restenosis identified by postmortem microcomputed tomography and histologic examination."
      },
